<title>MALAYSIA: GENERAL SOIL DEBUTS AT 7.9 RINGGIT.</title>
<headline>GENERAL SOIL DEBUTS AT 7.9 RINGGIT.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of General Soil Engineering Holdings Bhd made their debut on the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange at 7.90 ringgit each against an offer price of 2.70 ringgit.</p>
<p>General Soil, a specialist engineering contractor and property developer, offered 3.37 million existing and 550,000 new shares as part of its listing process</p>
<p>The company has forecast a net profit of 5.53 million ringgit for 1997 against 4.07 million last year.</p>
<p>At the debut price of 7.90 ringgit, the share is at a price-to-earnings multiple of 35.8 against 12.25 at the offer price.</p>
